# PG FINDER — COMPLETE PG OWNER DASHBOARD FUNCTIONALITY AND UI IMPROVEMENTS

## 1. Objective

Act as a senior full-stack developer, product designer, database architect, and mobile application engineer.

You are working on the existing PG Finder application.

Your task is to improve the existing PG Owner Dashboard and all associated property management modules according to the requirements below.

The application is intended for Indian PG owners, including people who may have limited technical knowledge or digital literacy.

Therefore, the application must be extremely easy to understand and operate.

Prioritize functionality, simplicity, accessibility, and professional design.

## 2. Strict implementation instructions

- Do not rebuild the application from scratch.
- Do not remove existing working functionality.
- Do not modify the Tenant Dashboard unnecessarily.
- Do not redesign the Super Admin Dashboard unnecessarily.
- Make supporting Super Admin changes only where required for owner workflows.
- Preserve the existing application architecture.
- Preserve existing authentication and authorization.
- Preserve the current Light, Dark, and System themes.
- Preserve the existing colors and design system.
- Preserve existing routes wherever possible.
- Reuse existing components.
- Do not create duplicate pages.
- Do not create disconnected mock datasets.
- All related modules must use consistent shared data.
- Do not introduce unnecessary animations.
- Keep the interface compact and professional.
- Every button must perform its intended action.
- Do not represent mock functionality as production-ready functionality.

Before making changes, inspect the existing PG Owner Dashboard, routes, components, services, state management, database models, and backend implementation.

