## 25. Privacy-preserving location sharing requests

Implement an administrator-reviewed location sharing request workflow for legitimate tenant assistance and safety-related purposes.

This feature must not be a surveillance or continuous tenant tracking system.

Do not silently collect tenant GPS coordinates.

Do not collect location automatically during login, logout, app opening, background activity, or ordinary tenant usage.

Do not interpret Last Active as a physical location.

Last Active may represent an application activity timestamp only.

### Owner request

Allow an authorized owner to submit a request for a tenant to voluntarily share a location.

The owner must have a legitimate relationship with the tenant through an eligible stay.

Request fields:

- Request ID
- Property
- Tenant
- Request Category
- Reason for Request
- Additional Explanation
- Request Timestamp
- Requested Access Duration

The owner must not receive any coordinates when submitting the request.

### Super Admin review

Send the request to an authorized administrator.

The administrator reviews:

- Owner identity
- Owner's relationship with the tenant
- Request purpose
- Request history
- Applicable privacy restrictions
- Whether the request is appropriate

Actions:

- Review
- Approve forwarding the request
- Reject
- Request additional information

Administrative approval only authorizes sending the request to the tenant.

It must not automatically disclose private location information.

### Tenant permission

After appropriate administrative review, notify the tenant.

Explain:

- Who is requesting the location
- Why it is requested
- What information would be shared
- How long access would last
- How to decline or revoke permission

Allow the tenant to:

- Accept and voluntarily share
- Decline
- Revoke access

Use additional protections for minors and vulnerable users.

Disable owner access to precise location for minors by default.

